[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 395,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 228,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57929,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 228,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myolipoma of soft tissue is a benign extrauterine tumour composed of mature adipose tissue and well-differentiated smooth muscle cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 396,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 229,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57930,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 229,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8890/0 Myolipoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 397,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 230,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57931,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 230,
        "headingText": "<p>2E80.01 &amp; XH4VB4 Deep subfascial lipoma &amp; Angiomyolipoma</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-01-23T15:18:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 398,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 231,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57932,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 231,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> extrauterine lipoleiomyoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 399,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 232,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57933,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 232,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 400,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 233,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57934,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 233,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myolipoma usually presents as a deeply situated mass within the retroperitoneum, abdominal cavity, pelvic cavity, or inguinal region. Less commonly it occurs in the trunk wall or extremities {27635945; 1703396; 7959650}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 401,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 234,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57935,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 234,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lesions within the abdominal cavity are often found incidentally, whereas those involving the trunk or extremities are palpable {27635945; 1703396}. MRI shows a fatty mass with associated signal-rich areas (corresponding to the smooth muscle component) that are heterogeneous on T1 postcontrast fat-suppressed images {17325918}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 402,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 235,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57936,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 235,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myolipoma is a rare tumour occurring chiefly in adult women. It is not associated with tuberous sclerosis {27635945; 1703396; 7959650}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 403,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 236,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57937,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 236,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 404,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 237,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57938,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 237,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cytogenetic alterations of the <em>HMGA2</em> gene have been reported in two cases {26857357; 12419585}. Fusion of the <em>HMGA2</em> and <em>C9orf92</em> genes resulting from a t(9;12)(p22;q14) has been reported in one case of myolipoma {26857357}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 411,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 244,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57939,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 244,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Deep myolipomas are frequently large, often reaching 10&ndash;25&nbsp;cm in size. Superficial lesions are smaller. The tumour is well circumscribed and usually surrounded by a thin capsule. The cut surface shows an admixture of yellowish adipose tissue and tan-whitish whorled nodules, depending on the amount and distribution of the smooth muscle component {27635945; 1703396; 7959650}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 405,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 238,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57940,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 238,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesions are composed of an intimate admixture of mature fat cells and spindled cells, in variable proportions. The spindled areas consist of well-differentiated smooth muscle, with intersecting fascicles of amitotic, cytologically bland cells having eosinophilic cytoplasm, cigar-shaped nuclei, and perinuclear vacuoles. The adipocytic component lacks any features to suggest atypical lipomatous tumour&nbsp;/ well-differentiated liposarcoma (e.g. enlarged atypical nuclei, fibrous septation, lipoblasts) {27635945; 1703396; 7959650}. The lesions usually contain variable numbers of small blood vessels and uterine thick-walled vessels {27635945}. Immunohistochemically, desmin, caldesmon, and SMA positivity confirms smooth muscle differentiation. Nuclear positivity for HMGA2 is identified in 60% of cases. ER and PR are often positive. MDM2, CDK4, and HMB45 are negative {27635945; 1703396; 8872156; 25517956; 15144408}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 406,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 239,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57941,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 239,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 407,
